  "bug_discussion": "Official fixing record: https://www.sqlite.org/src/info/26f39ac806a5582fab1497e38a4ce68dad2b79df8c8aade43c4e21eed7576931\n\nAdd the SQLITE_PREPARE_FROM_DDL flag to sqlite3_prepare_v3(). Use this to prevent fts3/4 tables in non-trusted schemas from calling unsafe SQL functions.\n\nFossilOrigin-Name: 26f39ac806a5582fab1497e38a4ce68dad2b79df8c8aade43c4e21eed7576931\n\nPreliminary source observation: FTS3/4 became innocuous in 2023, allowing use in non-trusted schemas. Internal FTS4 SQL then prepared unsafe application functions as top-level statements. The December 2025 fix sets SQLITE_PREPARE_FROM_DDL; its tests check the unsafe function is not invoked. A researcher published a retrospective analysis in March 2026, after the fix; its CVE label is unverified.\nSecurity impact, input reachability, earliest effective fix, and a three-revision oracle require independent review.",
